Description: Don't let VLC's request bursts stall browsing
 VLC for Android, when it shows a folder, lists every subfolder and fetches
 every advertised cover. Live folders advertised a cover URL for every
 folder (looked up only when fetched), so right after a restart VLC opened
 dozens of connections at once, each needing an uncached directory lookup.
 Requests are served one at a time and the listen backlog was 16: the
 kernel dropped connections (TcpExtListenDrops), VLC's own request to open
 the folder the user tapped was among them, and its SYN retries back off to
 a minute or more ("Loading" forever).
 .
  - listen() backlog is SOMAXCONN, so bursts wait in line instead of being
    dropped.
  - A folder gets a cover URL only once it is known to hold a cover file:
    listing a folder reveals that for free, and it is remembered next to
    its entry count (both checked against the folder's mtime).
  - Browses wait for probes out of a credit that refills at a tenth of real
    time (capped at probe_time), so a burst of subfolder listings barely
    waits while a single tap still gets the full probe_time; probes for a
    played or selected file jump the queue.
 .
 On a Raspberry Pi 4 with 245 subfolders: no dropped connections under a
 48-way cover flood, the subfolder pass takes 5.7 s instead of 68.8 s, and
 opening a folder meanwhile takes 0.02 s.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
